1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Recommendation feeds learn us for years,
then new accounts make us start over.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:14,500
For people switching accounts or platforms,
Curate turns that taste into a portable Passport.

3
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:21,500
I describe what I want naturally: less ragebait
and more science,

4
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:28,000
or an exact mix across astronomy, coding,
drawing, anime, and fragrance.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,000
I paste a few YouTube and Bluesky links.
Notes are optional.

6
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:40,500
Curate shows both platforms before and after,
with calmer content and more variety,

7
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:45,000
and a measurable drop in ragebait.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,500
The local Strands agent builds the plan, runs it in a safe
practice feed, and measures the result,

9
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:57,500
then restores the starting state.

10
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:05,500
The same Passport can be copied from one app to another;
Curate shows what carries over

11
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:10,500
and what needs a different route.

12
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:17,500
Incognito creates a temporary feed for a conference
or deep-work session,

13
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:21,500
then expires automatically or closes immediately.

14
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:27,000
A shared view can blend selected tastes with another
person without merging accounts.

15
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,500
Natural language in, a feed that feels like yours out,
and a way back.
